diff --git a/.github/patches/0004-Fix-duplicate-Seerr-requests-on-repeat-clicks.patch b/.github/patches/0004-Fix-duplicate-Seerr-requests-on-repeat-clicks.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bd77b94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/patches/0004-Fix-duplicate-Seerr-requests-on-repeat-clicks.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,198 @@
+From c9c95dea7ca8545931e3e06f4d8b4eec9497cd04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Vaibhav <vgupta1192@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:56:42 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 04/16] Fix duplicate Seerr requests on repeat clicks
+
+Seerr's own POST /api/v1/request duplicate check is a non-atomic
+SELECT-then-INSERT with no DB constraint - live testing showed two
+taps on the same title 22s apart both created separate requests
+instead of the second hitting a 409.
+
+requestMedia() now guards against duplicates before ever POSTing:
+1. In-memory 30s lock per tmdbId+mediaType (instant, catches repeat
+   taps)
+2. Pre-check against Seerr's GET /movie or /tv endpoint for existing
+   AVAILABLE/PENDING/APPROVED state (catches prior-process-lifetime
+   requests)
+
+Pre-check uses its own 3s timeout on a separate axios instance -
+the first version shared the 15s timeout with everything else and
+was missing the /api/v1 prefix on its path, causing /request to
+occasionally take 20+ seconds and 502 while it hung.
+
+Verified live: rapid repeat requests for the same title resolve in
+~3s then ~0.4s, and Seerr shows exactly one request created.
