+From 6f3e90885861b7649210b6b82fbf954f8d768aa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Vaibhav <vgupta1192@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:57:27 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 07/16] Add a dedicated Adult catalog, scoped separately from
+ Movies/Series
+
+Jellyfin's Adult library was previously a bare folder with no
+CollectionType, so it never got scanned/matched against TheMovieDb -
+recreated (delete + re-add, since CollectionType can't be changed
+in-place) as CollectionType=movies with the same LibraryOptions as the
+Movies library, so it now gets proper metadata scanning like Movies/
+Shows always have.
+
+That alone would have made Adult's content bleed into the existing
+"Jellyfin Movies" catalog though: the catalog queries had no per-library
+scoping at all (Items?IncludeItemTypes=Movie with no ParentId searches
+every library on the server at once). Added ParentId scoping to
+searchItems(), a JELLYFIN_{MOVIES,SHOWS,ADULT}_LIBRARY_ID env var per
+library (systemd unit), and a new movie/adult catalog entry in
+manifest.js wired through a catalog-id -> libraryId map in addon.js.
+
+Verified live: three catalogs, no overlap - Jellyfin Movies (20 of 77),
+Adult (20, its own distinct titles), Jellyfin Series (19 of 24,
+unaffected).
+---
+ addon.js    | 16 ++++++++++++++--
+ jellyfin.js | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
+ manifest.js | 15 +++++++++++++++
+ 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
+
