+From 456abbe9f194b8ed4974e0715727eeea8e35a155 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Vaibhav <vgupta1192@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:23:04 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 09/16] Fix season/episode mismatches and missing episode lists
+ for messy libraries
+
+Two separate but related problems, both confirmed live on real content:
+
+1. Some already-downloaded episodes were unreachable because Jellyfin's
+   season/episode numbers didn't line up with what Stremio/Cinemeta asks
+   for:
+   - Blackadder: season 1 correctly split out (6 episodes), but seasons
+     2+ all landed in one "Season Unknown" bucket with continuous
+     absolute numbering (episode 7 = "S2E1"). Asking for season 2
+     directly failed since no season has that IndexNumber.
+   - The Long Ballad: all 46 episode files are named after the release
+     site instead of the show, so Jellyfin's parser extracted no episode
+     number at all (IndexNumber: null on every one) - nothing to match
+     against even though every episode is physically present.
+
+2. Series using the "jf<itemId>" fallback id (see previous commit) had no
+   episode list at all - defineMetaHandler returned no `videos` array, so
+   nothing tells Stremio's UI what episodes exist. A real-imdb-id series
+   gets this for free from Cinemeta merging its own response in, but
+   nothing else recognizes our custom id namespace, so those series
+   rendered as a bare "Play" button like a single movie instead of a
+   browsable season/episode list.
+
+Added getCanonicalEpisodeList() in jellyfin.js as the single source of
+truth both problems share: it assigns every episode of a series one
+(season, episode) pair, keeping real Jellyfin numbers where they're
+unique and trustworthy, and falling back to positional numbering
+(sorted by premiere date, then name) for anything unnumbered or
+colliding - synthetic unnumbered seasons get folded into one season
+past the last real one rather than disappearing. Guards against a messy
+batch release (a "complete series + movies" pack) assigning the same
+number to two different files from two different causes (a shared stray
+index, and an order-dependent collision between a real index and an
+earlier positional fallback) - confirmed live, 32 collisions in a 581-
+episode release resolved to 0.
+
+defineMetaHandler now builds `videos` from this list for every series
+(addon.js), and resolveEpisode (used by both defineStreamHandler and the
+Seerr-request-polling helpers) looks answers up from the exact same
+list, so the episode list Stremio sees and what streams actually
+resolve to can never disagree.
+
+Verified live: Blackadder S2E1 (previously "Request via Seerr" despite
+being downloaded) now plays; The Long Ballad S1E1 same; two jf-fallback
+series ("Our Interpreter", a 500+ episode anime complete pack) now show
+full, individually-playable episode lists instead of a bare Play button.
