+ Jellyfin metadata, add visibility logging for every fallback path
+
+Requested audit of all three libraries (Movies, Adult, Series) for the
+same class of issue fixed in the previous two commits. Found one more,
+confirmed live: defineStreamHandler accessed
+item.MediaSources[0].MediaStreams[0].DisplayTitle unconditionally. 6
+real, otherwise-playable files across Movies/Adult (Jellyfin has a
+MediaSource for them but MediaStreams - the per-track technical
+metadata - came back empty, likely an ffprobe failure/incomplete scan)
+crashed the whole stream request instead of just missing a label.
+Confirmed via direct reproduction: {"err":"handler error"} for one of
+them before the fix, real playable stream after. Same guard applied to
+buildJellyfinStreamUrl (the Seerr-request-polling path). All 24 series
+independently swept too (comparing Jellyfin's real per-series episode
+count against what the addon exposes) - all 24 already matched exactly
+thanks to the previous commit's fix, confirming it generalizes rather
+than only covering the 2 examples found manually.
+
+The requested "fix it automatically in future" piece isn't a separate
+feature - it's what the last three commits already do, since
+getCanonicalEpisodeList and this MediaStreams guard both run fresh on
+every request rather than being one-off patches for specific titles.
+Any future messy download hits the same fallback logic automatically.
+What WAS missing is visibility into when that's happening: added
+console.warn logging (stderr) at both fallback points - unnumbered/
+duplicate-numbered episodes landing on positional numbering, and movies/
+episodes missing MediaStreams - each naming the specific item and
+explaining what happened and why, so a real numbering or metadata
+problem is now observable in the logs instead of silently invisible
+even though the addon is working around it.
