+Subject: [PATCH 11/16] Stop rendering a broken black box for items with no
+ poster, self-heal in background
+
+Investigated the pitch-black catalog tiles the user reported (screenshot:
+PPPD-526, PPPD-528 in Adult). Confirmed via direct ffprobe on the actual
+file: "moov atom not found" / "Invalid data found when processing
+input" - these specific files are genuinely corrupted/incomplete
+downloads, the same 6 files already found to have empty MediaStreams in
+the previous commit. No thumbnail extraction (or reliable playback) is
+possible from a file ffmpeg itself can't open - re-downloading those
+specific files is the real fix, not something addon code can work
+around.
+
+The black box itself was a separate, fixable bug though: itemToMeta
+always pointed `poster` at Items/{id}/Images/Primary even when Jellyfin
+has no Primary image for that item at all, which 404s and renders as a
+broken image instead of Stremio's own no-poster placeholder. Now omits
+`poster` entirely when ImageTags.Primary is absent.
+
+For the "automatically fix it in future" part: added a fire-and-forget
+refreshItemImages() in jellyfin.js, triggered once per item per process
+lifetime the first time itemToMeta sees no Primary image. This asks
+Jellyfin to re-run its own already-configured image fetchers (embedded
+cover extraction, TheMovieDb, and "Screen Grabber" - a frame pulled
+directly from the video - as the last resort), not awaited or allowed to
+affect the response it was triggered from. Self-heals any future item
+that's a valid, readable file simply missing a downloaded poster;
+harmlessly no-ops forever for permanently unreadable files like the 6
+found here.
+
+Also added ImageTags to the two Items list-endpoint queries that were
+missing it (Fields=ProviderIds,MediaSources was already needed for the
+season/media fixes in prior commits - list responses omit ImageTags too
+unless explicitly requested, same lesson as ProviderIds).
