+Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:12:15 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 14/16] fix: persist adultItemIds to disk so the Seerr
+ exclusion survives restarts
+
+adultItemIds was in-memory only, populated when the Adult catalog gets
+listed, on the assumption the catalog would always be re-listed before
+a user could click into a title from it within the same process
+lifetime. That assumption breaks on every restart of this addon (log
+rotation, deploys, etc. restart it periodically) - a title already
+known to be Adult from a browse before the restart lost that
+protection the moment the process restarted, since the Set came back
+empty and Stremio doesn't necessarily re-list the catalog before
+reopening a title it already has cached client-side. Confirmed live as
+the reported bug: "Request via Seerr" showing for Adult content that's
+no longer found in Jellyfin (e.g. deleted after watching), right after
+an addon restart.
+
+Now loads/saves the same Set to data/adult-item-ids.json (gitignored)
+instead of keeping it in-memory only, so the exclusion survives
+restarts. Verified live: browsed the Adult catalog (20 items recorded),
+restarted the service, confirmed the file's 20 entries survived intact
+and are reloaded into the running process.
+
